Boost 1.72 mpl: route integral_c's next/prior through the enum-safe step.

The companion to mpl_integral_wrapper_step.patch. Where the step helper is
available (C++11 and later) next/prior are computed through it; otherwise the
original expressions are kept byte-for-byte, so pre-C++11 compilers and every
platform that does not define BOOST_MPL_AUX_ENUM_SAFE_STEP build exactly the
code they built before.

The fallback branch is respelled (value+1) rather than (value + 1) so that the
replaced text does not occur in the replacement: base.apply_patch is a plain
textual substitution with no record of having run, and boost.py re-applies it
on every make.py. Without the respelling a second application would nest the
conditional inside its own #else and produce an #elif after an #else.

